00:00:54.465 --> 00:00:55.281
And I received.

00:00:55.281 --> 00:00:57.721
&gt;&gt; Thanks for the buzz.

00:00:57.721 --> 00:01:00.120
I'm so glad you know I still have buzz.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.233
So good.

00:01:02.233 --> 00:01:04.758
&gt;&gt; I received a lot of support and advice
from my

00:01:04.758 --> 00:01:07.762
friends and that was really great and I
just wanted to

00:01:07.762 --> 00:01:10.902
say I think the best advice I've heard was
don't worry

00:01:10.902 --> 00:01:14.749
Amanda, if you mess up, Oprah can just
interview herself [LAUGH].

00:01:14.749 --> 00:01:16.479
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH] So, if I falter, feel free to

00:01:16.479 --> 00:01:19.620
ask yourself some questions, and we'll,
and we'll be good.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:22.660
[LAUGH] But to get things started, I want,
I

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:27.296
thought we'd frame today's talk with
framing three sections with

00:01:27.296 --> 00:01:30.716
quotes of yours that you shared after
wrapping up your

00:01:30.716 --> 00:01:34.440
25th season and final season of the Oprah
Winfrey Show.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:40.040
And I thought some of these quotes, I mean
you share so much wisdom but, these these

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:45.247
really spoke to me, and thought would be a
great way to frame our discussion.

00:01:45.247 --> 00:01:45.363
&gt;&gt; Okay.

00:01:45.363 --> 00:01:48.448
&gt;&gt; So this first one that I will read for
everyone

00:01:48.448 --> 00:01:51.693
and for you so you don't have to strain
your neck

00:01:51.693 --> 00:01:55.100
is you have to know what sparks the light
in you

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:59.020
so that you, in your own way, can
illuminate the world.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:00.910
So I wanted to take this time to talk

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:04.570
about your early career and how you
discovered your calling.

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:07.440
So lets go back to when you were college
age.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:13.200
Did you know that you wanted to get into
TV and media specifically?

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.230
&gt;&gt; No I did not.

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:17.140
I thought that I was going to be a
teacher.

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:23.130
I was in my Sophomore class at Tennessee
State University.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:28.726
I'd already been working in radio since I
was 16 and my

00:02:28.726 --> 00:02:35.310
I remember I was in Mr. Cox's drawing
class for theatre.

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:36.670
And I was terrible drawer.

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:38.993
He said, I couldn't draw a straight line
with a ruler.

00:02:38.993 --> 00:02:41.163
[LAUGH] And and I got a call in that
class, from a guy at the local

00:02:41.163 --> 00:02:43.950
station CBS, and he have been calling me
several times when I was working in radio.

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:50.680
So I started working in radio at 16, and
one

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:56.570
of them is fire prevention contest,
another one story.

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:58.890
And so when I went back to the station to
pick my

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:02.770
prize, some guy said, would you like to
hear your voice on tape.

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:07.610
I said sure and I started reading this
copy on tape.

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:10.610
They called everybody in the building,
said here this kid read.

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:12.600
I was 16 they hired me in radio.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.678
So I was in radio at 16.

00:03:14.678 --> 00:03:21.840
And so I started getting calls about my
freshman year to come into television.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.350
I had never thought about it.

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:26.165
And still was living at home, and couldn't

00:03:26.165 --> 00:03:29.209
figure out how I'd manage those, I had
biology

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:34.783
at 1 o'clock, and so I couldn't figure out
how I would be able to manage my schedule.

00:03:34.783 --> 00:03:37.981
[COUGH] And Mr. Cox said to me, the one
same, same

00:03:37.981 --> 00:03:42.330
professor said you can't draw a straight
line with a ruler.

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:47.960
He said, I came back from, from taking
this phone call and

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:52.317
he said who was that I said there's this
guy at CBS

00:03:52.317 --> 00:03:57.312
he keeps calling me, he wants me to
interview for a job,

00:03:57.312 --> 00:04:02.055
and Mr. Cox said, that is why you go to
school fool.

00:04:02.055 --> 00:04:04.020
[LAUGHING] So that CBS can call you.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:06.090
[LAUGH] That is why you are in school.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:09.940
So I, he said you, you leave now and go
call him back.

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:11.530
And, and, I did.

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:14.945
And I was hired in television not knowing
anything about it.

00:04:14.945 --> 00:04:17.030
&gt;&gt; Mm-hm.

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:19.480
&gt;&gt; Having in mind Barbera Walters but
thinking.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.818
Oh, okay I can do that.

00:04:21.818 --> 00:04:23.890
Not knowing how to write or film or
anything.

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:24.610
&gt;&gt; Mm-hm.

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:29.675
&gt;&gt; And I think it was because it was the,
it was the times and I literally had

00:04:29.675 --> 00:04:35.521
somebody who was willing to work with me
that I, that I managed to, to find my way.

00:04:35.521 --> 00:04:38.854
But I had to find my way, because, the
reporting

00:04:38.854 --> 00:04:42.250
never really fit me, and what did work for
me.

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:45.610
I'm this old, I'm so old that when I

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:48.725
started that it was the year of live
action cam.

00:04:48.725 --> 00:04:55.093
[COUGH] And so, it was like video cameras
live, and so, the news stations would do

00:04:55.093 --> 00:04:57.902
a live, a live shot they would throw

00:04:57.902 --> 00:05:01.570
to somebody live even if nothing was going
on.

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:01.720
&gt;&gt; Right.

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:02.650
&gt;&gt; Just so they could say live action cam.

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:06.853
And what I found was I wasn't so good at
the writing part but if

00:05:06.853 --> 00:05:12.557
I was just standing up and talking about
what had just happened it was really good.

00:05:12.557 --> 00:05:15.597
And then I started to feel, so I started

00:05:15.597 --> 00:05:21.506
at 19 working in television, became an
anchor immediately afterwards.

00:05:21.506 --> 00:05:23.863
My father still had an 11 o'clock curfew.

00:05:23.863 --> 00:05:25.373
Can you believe such a thing?

00:05:25.373 --> 00:05:28.053
[LAUGH] That I am, that I am

00:05:28.053 --> 00:05:34.197
the 10 o'clock anchor [LAUGH] in Nashville
Tennessee.

00:05:34.197 --> 00:05:36.866
I am the woman on the newscast.

00:05:36.866 --> 00:05:40.171
[LAUGH] Reading the news, and my father
would say be home by 11.

00:05:40.171 --> 00:05:43.757
[LAUGH] And I'd say, dad, the news is on
at ten,

00:05:43.757 --> 00:05:47.816
he goes and it's off at 10:30 so be home
by 11.

00:05:47.816 --> 00:05:49.790
[LAUGH] So I, I, I had a very strict
Gracier father.

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:55.400
So, anyway, I, I could feel inside myself,
that reporting was

00:05:55.400 --> 00:06:00.920
not the right thing for me even though I
was happy to have the job.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:01.070
&gt;&gt; Right.

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:02.890
&gt;&gt; I got an offer to go to Atlanta.

00:06:02.890 --> 00:06:06.153
I was making $10,000 a year in 1971, but
still

00:06:06.153 --> 00:06:09.970
in college, so I was thinking I was doing
pretty good.

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:10.090
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:14.102
&gt;&gt; I got an offer to go to Atlanta for
$40,000 which I thought.

00:06:14.102 --> 00:06:15.141
It's over.

00:06:15.141 --> 00:06:19.204
[LAUGH] I'm gonna make $40,000.

00:06:19.204 --> 00:06:24.273
And my boss at the time said to me you do
not know what you don't know.

00:06:24.273 --> 00:06:24.576
&gt;&gt; Mm-hm.

00:06:24.576 --> 00:06:27.625
&gt;&gt; And you need to stay here until you can
learn to

00:06:27.625 --> 00:06:33.670
write better until you can can perfect
your craft as, as a journalist.

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:38.110
And so I, I he said we can't give you 40,
but we can give you 12.

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:40.600
So [LAUGH] so I stayed and you know the
reason why I stayed is cuz I could

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:41.890
feel inside myself that even though the 40
was

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:47.100
alluring at the time, that he was
absolutely right.

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:50.304
So to make a long story short, cuz I'd be

00:06:50.304 --> 00:06:54.563
here all day just talking about how it all
came about.

00:06:54.563 --> 00:06:59.877
I started listening, to what felt like the
truth for me.

00:06:59.877 --> 00:07:00.638
&gt;&gt; Mm-hm.

00:07:00.638 --> 00:07:03.137
&gt;&gt; A couple of years later I moved to
Baltimore.

00:07:03.137 --> 00:07:09.093
I could feel that as a reporter, and by
this time, 22, I'm making 22,000.

00:07:09.093 --> 00:07:11.561
I met my best friend Gale there who said
oh my

00:07:11.561 --> 00:07:15.950
god, can you imagine when your thirty and
your making 30,000.

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:18.623
[LAUGH] And then you're 40 and then it's
40,000.

00:07:18.623 --> 00:07:26.967
[LAUGH] We actually had that conversation
in the bathroom.

00:07:26.967 --> 00:07:33.570
So this is I started to feel that
reporting wasn't for me.

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:35.120
But I had my father, I had my friends.

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:38.950
Everybody was saying, oh my God, you're,
you're an anchorwoman, you're on TV.

00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:40.487
I mean, you can't give up that job.

00:07:40.487 --> 00:07:40.860
&gt;&gt; Right.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.374
&gt;&gt; And when I was, by the time I was

00:07:42.374 --> 00:07:45.540
making 25, my father goes, you just hit
the jackpot.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:46.570
You not gonna make no more money than
that.

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:47.150
That's just it.

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:49.470
So I was torn between what the world was
saying

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:52.840
to me, and what I felt to be the truth for

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:55.570
myself.

00:07:55.570 --> 00:08:00.080
It felt like an unnatural act for me
reporting, although

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:02.450
I knew that to a lot of people, it was
glamorous.

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:06.475
And, I started to just inside myself think
what, what

00:08:06.475 --> 00:08:09.810
do I really wanna do, what I really wanna
do.

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:10.510
And I will say this.

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:14.710
Knowing what you don't want to do is the
best

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:16.550
possible place to be if you don't know
what to do.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:19.190
Because knowing what you don't want to do
leads you to

00:08:19.190 --> 00:08:21.090
figure out what it is that you really do
wanna do.

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:21.640
&gt;&gt; Okay.

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:22.750
So you discovered talk then, right?

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:25.820
Around that time?

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:26.351
&gt;&gt; I didn't discover talk.

00:08:26.351 --> 00:08:27.970
I was being, I got demoted.

00:08:27.970 --> 00:08:28.590
&gt;&gt; God.

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:33.140
&gt;&gt; They wanted to fire me but I was, I was
under contract.

00:08:33.140 --> 00:08:35.750
They didn't wanna give up the 25,000 so
they were

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:38.040
trying to keep me on to the end of the
year.

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:42.244
So they put me on the, this is how life
works, [CROSSTALK]

00:08:42.244 --> 00:08:45.732
they put me on a talk show to try and
avoid having

00:08:45.732 --> 00:08:49.219
to pay me the contract out and the moment
I sat on

00:08:49.219 --> 00:08:55.145
the talk show interviewing the Carvel ice
cream man and his multiple flavors.

00:08:55.145 --> 00:08:59.110
[LAUGH] I knew that I had found home for
myself.

00:08:59.110 --> 00:09:05.389
Because when I was a news reporter, it was
so unnatural for me, I, you know, to cover

00:09:05.389 --> 00:09:11.690
somebody's tragedies and difficulties and
then to not to have feel anything for it.

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:13.297
And I would go back after a fire.

00:09:13.297 --> 00:09:13.589
&gt;&gt; Mm-hm.

00:09:13.589 --> 00:09:15.978
&gt;&gt; And I would take the blankets and then
I would get

00:09:15.978 --> 00:09:18.800
a note from my boss saying, what the hell
are you doing?

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:19.210
&gt;&gt; Right.

00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:20.360
&gt;&gt; You're just supposed to report on it.

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:21.220
&gt;&gt; Can't be that empathetic.

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:22.850
&gt;&gt; Can, cannot be that empathetic.

00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:23.580
And it felt unnatural for me.

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:30.150
So if I were to put it in business terms,
if it were were to leave you with a

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:37.371
message, that the truth is I have from the
very beginning listened to my instinct.

00:09:37.371 --> 00:09:43.067
All of my best decisions in life have come
because I was

00:09:43.067 --> 00:09:49.980
attuned to what really felt like the next
right move for me.

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:52.100
And so, it didn't feel right.

00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:54.250
I knew that I wouldn't be there forever.

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:57.871
I never even learned the street in
Baltimore, because I thought I was there

00:09:57.871 --> 00:10:01.850
longer than I thought, I was there eight
years I should've learned the streets.

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:04.049
[CROSSTALK] I kept saying to myself I'm
not gonna be here long, I'm not

00:10:04.049 --> 00:10:06.338
gonna be here, I'm not gonna be here so
I'm not gonna learn the street.

00:10:06.338 --> 00:10:08.754
So when I got the call to come to Chicago.

00:10:08.754 --> 00:10:10.055
&gt;&gt; Mm-hm.

00:10:10.055 --> 00:10:14.514
&gt;&gt; After you know starting with a, with a
coanchor and, and working in

00:10:14.514 --> 00:10:19.040
talk, for several years, I knew that it
was the right thing to do.

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:22.380
And I knew that if I didn't even if I,
didn't succeed cuz

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:26.013
at the time, there was a, there was a guy
named Phil Donahue.

00:10:26.013 --> 00:10:26.267
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:10:26.267 --> 00:10:27.535
&gt;&gt; Who was the king of talk.

00:10:27.535 --> 00:10:28.800
&gt;&gt; Mm-hm.

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:32.312
And was on in Chicago, and every single
person,

00:10:32.312 --> 00:10:36.180
except my best friend Gale, said you are
gonna fail.

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:39.872
Every single person, [INAUDIBLE] my bosses
by this time thought I was

00:10:39.872 --> 00:10:44.430
terrific, and said, you're gonna, you're,
you're waking into a land mine.

00:10:44.430 --> 00:10:45.360
You're gonna fail.

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:47.060
You're gonna fail.

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:48.022
Chicago's a racist city.

00:10:48.022 --> 00:10:49.806
You're black you're not gonna make it.

00:10:49.806 --> 00:10:51.553
Everything to, to keep me same.

00:10:51.553 --> 00:10:56.127
Then they offered me a car and apartment
and all this stuff, and I said no.

00:10:56.127 --> 00:11:00.090
If I fail, then I will find out what is
the next thing for me.

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:00.240
&gt;&gt; Right.

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:01.430
&gt;&gt; What is the next true thing for me.

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:04.090
&gt;&gt; It felt right to you, so you went for
it.

00:11:04.090 --> 00:11:08.160
&gt;&gt; Cuz it felt like this is now the move I
need to make.

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:09.610
And I was not one of those people you

00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:11.660
know, all of my the people who worked with
me

00:11:11.660 --> 00:11:13.810
in the news, they would have their taps
and they'd

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:17.090
have their stories, and they'd have you
know resume's ready.

00:11:17.090 --> 00:11:20.079
I didn't have any of that, cuz I knew that
the time would come.

00:11:20.079 --> 00:11:20.364
&gt;&gt; Mm-hm.

00:11:20.364 --> 00:11:23.180
&gt;&gt; Where I would, where what I needed
would show up for me.

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:23.560
&gt;&gt; Okay.

00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:25.440
&gt;&gt; And when that showed up, I was ready.

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:27.898
Because my definition of luck, is

00:11:27.898 --> 00:11:32.180
preparation meeting the moment of
opportunity.

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:32.581
&gt;&gt; Right.

00:11:32.581 --> 00:11:36.535
&gt;&gt; And I was prepared to be able to step
into that, that, that

00:11:36.535 --> 00:11:40.320
world of talk in a way that I, I knew I
could do it.

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:41.150
&gt;&gt; Great.

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:45.440
So, often in your career I'm sure you were
a minority.

00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:47.560
Perhaps as the only woman.

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:52.290
The only black person, the only person
from a poor family.

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:55.030
Did this pr, affect you on your
professional path?

00:11:55.030 --> 00:11:59.490
And how did you navigate situations in
which you might have felt more alone?

00:11:59.490 --> 00:11:59.550
&gt;&gt; Hm.

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:01.120
&gt;&gt; And now how did that impact how you
lead and

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:03.430
how you might help people who may be
feeling that same thing?

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:09.745
&gt;&gt; Okay, that's a lot of questions.

00:12:09.745 --> 00:12:10.150
[LAUGH].

00:12:10.150 --> 00:12:11.250
&gt;&gt; I'm sorry, all right let's let's-.

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:12.853
&gt;&gt; Let me put my glasses on.

00:12:12.853 --> 00:12:14.098
[LAUGH].

00:12:14.098 --> 00:12:19.520
&gt;&gt; I figured I had you here, I was gonna,
I was gonna ask as much as I can.

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:22.740
&gt;&gt; Oh, Amanda went deep on me for a minute
there.

00:12:22.740 --> 00:12:23.650
Whoa.

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:25.765
Back up sister girl, c'mon, back up.

00:12:25.765 --> 00:12:27.352
[LAUGH] So first one is.

00:12:27.352 --> 00:12:31.120
&gt;&gt; So how did you navigate in which you
would have felt more-

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:35.460
&gt;&gt; Always the only, only woman walk in the
room-

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:36.039
&gt;&gt; Mm-hm.

00:12:36.039 --> 00:12:43.740
&gt;&gt; Still and there is a room full of white
men, usually older thrills me.

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:44.388
Just thrills me.

00:12:44.388 --> 00:12:47.840
[LAUGHING] I just, I just love it.

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:53.429
[LAUGHING] Usually the only black person
in the room.

00:12:53.429 --> 00:12:57.869
Also, never really concerned me because I,
I don't look at people through color.

00:12:57.869 --> 00:12:59.998
I didn't get to be where I am by, and,

00:12:59.998 --> 00:13:03.204
who I am, by looking at the color of
people's skin.

00:13:03.204 --> 00:13:07.000
I really, literally, took Martin Luther
King at his word.

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:08.510
and, understand that the content of a
person's character,

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:15.970
and, refuse to let anybody else do that to
me.

00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:16.575
So, I love it, just love it.

00:13:16.575 --> 00:13:23.774
And there's a wonderful phrase by Maya
Angelou, from a poem that she wrote called

00:13:23.774 --> 00:13:30.431
To Our Grandmothers, that she says, when I
come as one but I stand as 10,000.

00:13:30.431 --> 00:13:32.550
[COUGH] So when I walk into a room and

00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:36.569
particularly before I have something
really challenging to do

00:13:36.569 --> 00:13:39.144
or I'm gonna be in a circumstance where I

00:13:39.144 --> 00:13:43.342
feel I'm going to be you know, against
some difficulties.

00:13:43.342 --> 00:13:47.094
I would literally sit, and I would call on
the 10,000.

00:13:47.094 --> 00:13:47.660
&gt;&gt; Mm-hm.

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:51.400
&gt;&gt; I would call on back to the ancestors,I
would call on

00:13:51.400 --> 00:13:55.905
those people who come before me, call on
those women who forged

00:13:55.905 --> 00:13:58.880
a path that I might be able to sit in the
room

00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:02.453
with all of those white men, and I love it
so much.

00:14:02.453 --> 00:14:03.465
[LAUGH] I, I call on, I call on that.

00:14:03.465 --> 00:14:03.945
&gt;&gt; Right.

00:14:03.945 --> 00:14:10.249
&gt;&gt; Because I know that my being where I
am, and first of all, being who I am and

00:14:10.249 --> 00:14:14.115
where I am didn't come just out of myself
that

00:14:14.115 --> 00:14:17.494
I come from a heritage and so I own that.

00:14:17.494 --> 00:14:18.051
&gt;&gt; Mm-hm.

00:14:18.051 --> 00:14:20.550
&gt;&gt; And I step into that room not just as

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:24.520
myself but I bring all of that, that,
energy with me.

00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:27.644
So it has never been an issue for me
except when

00:14:27.644 --> 00:14:33.004
I was, I think, 23, still working in,
still working in Baltimore.

00:14:33.004 --> 00:14:33.435
&gt;&gt; Mm-hm.

00:14:33.435 --> 00:14:39.424
&gt;&gt; I'd gone to my boss and said that the
guy who was working with me, co, co,

00:14:39.424 --> 00:14:45.520
my cohost on the People Are Talking show,
was making more money than I.

00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:47.661
And we were, we were cohosts.

00:14:47.661 --> 00:14:54.132
So I went to my boss and I said, this was
in 1970, I was older than

00:14:54.132 --> 00:15:00.961
23, this was 1979, 80, and I said I, I
just would like to-.

00:15:00.961 --> 00:15:03.495
You know how intimidating it is to go to
the boss in the first place.

00:15:03.495 --> 00:15:06.450
[INAUDIBLE] But I'm gonna go, and I'm
gonna stand up for myself.

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:09.567
[LAUGH] And, I said, Richard's making more
money than I am, and I,

00:15:09.567 --> 00:15:12.976
and I, and I don't think that's fair
because we're doing the same job.

00:15:12.976 --> 00:15:13.907
We sit in the same show.

00:15:13.907 --> 00:15:14.887
We do the same.

00:15:14.887 --> 00:15:20.326
And, my general manager said, why, why
should you make as much money as he?

00:15:20.326 --> 00:15:22.420
And I said, cuz we're doing the same job.

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:25.360
And he said but he has children.

00:15:27.390 --> 00:15:28.930
[LAUGH] Do you have children?

00:15:28.930 --> 00:15:30.110
And I said no.

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:32.480
He said, well he has to pay for college
educations.

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:33.930
So he has, he owns his own home.

00:15:33.930 --> 00:15:35.170
Do you own your home?

00:15:35.170 --> 00:15:36.590
I said no.

00:15:36.590 --> 00:15:40.200
He said, he has a mortgage to pay.

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:42.270
He has insurance, he has do you have that?

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:42.605
No.

00:15:42.605 --> 00:15:45.109
So, tell me, why, why do you need the same
amount of money?

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:48.410
And I said, thank you for your time.

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:50.960
And I left.

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:51.421
I left.

00:15:51.421 --> 00:15:53.200
I didn't complain about it.

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:56.306
I didn't file a, a, a, a suit about it.

00:15:56.306 --> 00:16:01.890
I knew, that in that moment, it was time
for me to go, and that I started the

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:07.403
process for myself, of preparing myself
for, you will not be here long.

00:16:07.403 --> 00:16:09.558
You are not gonna be able to get what you
need.

00:16:09.558 --> 00:16:15.747
I had a boss at the time who was African
American, and had just been

00:16:15.747 --> 00:16:22.450
for the first time, made an assistant news
director, and was drunk with power.

00:16:22.450 --> 00:16:27.067
Drunk with power, and felt it his, I
think, I don't know, I think

00:16:27.067 --> 00:16:31.690
he woke up in the morning thinking of
things he could do to harass me.

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:37.970
I decided not to file a suit against it,
cuz I knew, at the time, I would lose.

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:38.914
&gt;&gt; Right.

00:16:38.914 --> 00:16:43.439
&gt;&gt; That no good would come of it, that I
would be blackballed in television, that

00:16:43.439 --> 00:16:48.054
it would turn into a major thing, and I
knew, I didn't have long to stay there.

00:16:48.054 --> 00:16:53.392
I had a vision for what the future was,
even though I couldn't place

00:16:53.392 --> 00:16:58.652
exactly where my future would be, I knew
who held the future.

00:16:58.652 --> 00:17:02.646
Cuz I am really guided by a force that's
bigger than myself.

00:17:02.646 --> 00:17:05.926
I know that my being here on the planet is
not just of my own being.

00:17:05.926 --> 00:17:08.590
&gt;&gt; So you used that as momentum to just
leave, cut your losses and go.

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:10.571
&gt;&gt; No, I just [INAUDIBLE] and I filed it
away.

00:17:10.571 --> 00:17:11.237
&gt;&gt; [CROSSTALK] Yeah.

00:17:11.237 --> 00:17:11.886
&gt;&gt; There will come a time.

00:17:11.886 --> 00:17:13.532
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH] Huh, it's gonna come back.

00:17:13.532 --> 00:17:14.778
Yeah, you were right.

00:17:14.778 --> 00:17:15.498
I think you were right.

00:17:15.498 --> 00:17:17.425
&gt;&gt; When I will be sitting in the same
room.

00:17:17.425 --> 00:17:19.717
And it happened, like, in the late 90s.

00:17:19.717 --> 00:17:21.620
I had the Oprah show and I ran into that
guy.

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:23.642
Lord, Jesus, thank you.

00:17:23.642 --> 00:17:29.535
[LAUGH] [LAUGH] Oh my god.

00:17:29.535 --> 00:17:31.834
Oh, one of the sweetest moments I've ever
happened.

00:17:31.834 --> 00:17:34.237
[LAUGH] Oh, go ahead.

00:17:34.237 --> 00:17:35.042
&gt;&gt; Okay.

00:17:35.042 --> 00:17:36.868
[LAUGH] Here we go.

00:17:36.868 --> 00:17:39.134
So, right now, as we sit here, we're

00:17:39.134 --> 00:17:42.930
about five miles from Facebook and Sheryl
Sandberg.

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:44.840
And last year, she published the book Lean
In.

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:47.190
And it's gotten incredible traction.

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:50.120
It had some, you know, criticism as well.

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:53.400
And I was wondering if you were to write a
book on women in careers.

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:55.400
What would your title be?

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:57.724
&gt;&gt; Mine would be, actually.

00:17:57.724 --> 00:18:00.504
Mine wouldn't be lean in.

00:18:00.504 --> 00:18:06.386
It would be, step up and into yourself,
because, this is the truth.

00:18:06.386 --> 00:18:13.316
There is no real doing in the world,
without being first.

00:18:13.316 --> 00:18:16.659
For me, being.

00:18:16.659 --> 00:18:21.169
Your presence, your connection to
yourself, and that which is

00:18:21.169 --> 00:18:25.690
greater than yourself, is far more
important than what you do.

00:18:25.690 --> 00:18:28.110
But also, is the thing that fuels what you
do.

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:30.060
&gt;&gt; Right.

00:18:30.060 --> 00:18:36.394
&gt;&gt; And I know that one of the things that
is so important for what happens here.

00:18:36.394 --> 00:18:43.356
At the graduate school, is that you have
leaders who are self actualized,

00:18:43.356 --> 00:18:49.562
and understand what your contribution to
change the world can be.

00:18:49.562 --> 00:18:52.616
You can only do that, if you know
yourself.

00:18:52.616 --> 00:18:55.619
You can only do that, unless you take,
unless

00:18:55.619 --> 00:18:58.708
you, you cannot do it unless you take the
time.

00:18:58.708 --> 00:19:03.196
To actually know who you are, and why you
are here.

00:19:03.196 --> 00:19:09.908
Now, I happen to know, for sure, that
every human being comes, comes called.

00:19:09.908 --> 00:19:15.738
And that the calling goes beyond the
definition of what your job is.

00:19:15.738 --> 00:19:23.360
That there is innate, there is an innate,
supreme moment of destiny, for everybody.

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:26.505
And, that's why when I was in Baltimore, I
could feel, this isn't it.

00:19:26.505 --> 00:19:26.810
&gt;&gt; Mm-hm.

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:27.980
&gt;&gt; This isn't it.

00:19:27.980 --> 00:19:31.366
And then in Chicago after 25 years of
success

00:19:31.366 --> 00:19:34.278
on the show, I started to feel, this isn't

00:19:34.278 --> 00:19:38.529
it, there is something more, something
more, something more

00:19:38.529 --> 00:19:42.090
that's calling me to what is the supreme
moment.

00:19:42.090 --> 00:19:43.339
And everybody has that.

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:52.211
And you cannot fulfill it, unless you have
a level of self awareness, to be connected

00:19:52.211 --> 00:19:54.974
to what is the inner voice, or the

00:19:54.974 --> 00:19:59.342
instinct, I call it your emotional GPS
system.

00:19:59.342 --> 00:20:02.950
That allows you to make the best decisions
for yourself.

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:06.471
And every decision, that has profited me.

00:20:06.471 --> 00:20:06.944
&gt;&gt; Mm-hm.

00:20:06.944 --> 00:20:08.856
&gt;&gt; Has come from me listening to that

00:20:08.856 --> 00:20:11.589
inner voice first, and every deci, every
time

00:20:11.589 --> 00:20:13.913
I've gotten into a situation where I was

00:20:13.913 --> 00:20:16.870
in trouble, it's because I didn't listen
to it.

00:20:16.870 --> 00:20:22.578
I overrode that voice, that instinct, with
my own, with my own head, my own thinking.

00:20:22.578 --> 00:20:24.928
I tried to rationalize it, I tried to tell
myself.

00:20:24.928 --> 00:20:28.287
But, you know, okay, you're gonna make a
lot of money oh, no.

00:20:28.287 --> 00:20:33.577
And so, I am, I sit here you know,
profitable,

00:20:33.577 --> 00:20:38.645
successful, by all the definitions of the
world.

00:20:38.645 --> 00:20:43.880
But, what really, really, really resonates
deeply with me.

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:48.100
Is that I live, a fantastic life.

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:51.430
My inner life is really intact.

00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:53.360
My, I live from the inside out.

00:20:53.360 --> 00:21:00.050
And so, everything that I have, I have
because I let it be fueled by who I am.

00:21:00.050 --> 00:21:04.160
And what I realized my contributions to
the planet could be.

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:08.260
And what my real contribution is, it looks
like I'm a, I was a talk show host.

00:21:08.260 --> 00:21:10.430
It looks like, you know, I'm in the
movies.

00:21:10.430 --> 00:21:12.580
It looks like, you know, I have a network.

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:15.958
But my real contribution, the reason why
I'm

00:21:15.958 --> 00:21:19.518
here, is to help connect people to
themselves.

00:21:19.518 --> 00:21:22.657
And the higher ideas of consciousness.

00:21:22.657 --> 00:21:24.776
I'm here to help raise consciousness.

00:21:24.776 --> 00:21:28.800
So my television platform, was to help
raise consciousness.

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:30.009
At the beginning I didn't realize that.

00:21:30.009 --> 00:21:32.161
I thought, oh my God, I got a show!

00:21:32.161 --> 00:21:40.760
[LAUGH] And it wasn't until I was
interviewing the Ku Klux Klan one day.

00:21:40.760 --> 00:21:42.759
And, can you, imagine all the great
lessons

00:21:42.759 --> 00:21:46.080
come from things that are, that are
sometimes challenging.

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:48.527
I was interviewing Ku Klux Klan, and I

00:21:48.527 --> 00:21:51.664
thought, as an African American oh, I'm
gonna

00:21:51.664 --> 00:21:54.416
get them, I'm gonna show for every Jewish

00:21:54.416 --> 00:21:58.990
person, for every person who's been
discriminated against.

00:21:58.990 --> 00:22:02.001
And during the commercial break, I saw the

00:22:02.001 --> 00:22:05.857
klan exchanging signals and looks at each
other.

00:22:05.857 --> 00:22:11.773
And then something inside, that instinct,
I thought, I am doing nobody any good.

00:22:11.773 --> 00:22:13.222
They are loving this.

00:22:13.222 --> 00:22:15.163
They are using me.

00:22:15.163 --> 00:22:16.804
I think I'm doing an interview.

00:22:16.804 --> 00:22:18.851
They are using me.

00:22:18.851 --> 00:22:20.263
I did not know it at the time.

00:22:20.263 --> 00:22:25.007
I brought them on, actually, those same
guys back, in for my last year.

00:22:25.007 --> 00:22:28.955
And they told me, that they used that
show, for their recruitment.

00:22:28.955 --> 00:22:31.300
I could feel that happening.

00:22:31.300 --> 00:22:35.979
And I made a decision after that show,
I'll never do anything like that again.

00:22:35.979 --> 00:22:37.619
I'll never let my platform be used.

00:22:37.619 --> 00:22:38.155
&gt;&gt; Right.

00:22:38.155 --> 00:22:39.938
&gt;&gt; And I will not be used.

00:22:39.938 --> 00:22:42.554
And, at the time, in the 90s,

00:22:42.554 --> 00:22:47.987
early 90s, everybody was doing,
confrontational television.

00:22:47.987 --> 00:22:50.535
And I thought I was above the fray, cuz
I'm,

00:22:50.535 --> 00:22:53.767
cuz I'm not like like Jerry Springer, I
don't do that.

00:22:53.767 --> 00:22:59.340
[LAUGH] So in my egoic delusion, I thought
because I am not that bad.

00:22:59.340 --> 00:23:01.305
I'm really not bad.

00:23:01.305 --> 00:23:03.813
But I was doing confrontational
television.

00:23:03.813 --> 00:23:07.667
I thought I was exposing, men with
affairs.

00:23:07.667 --> 00:23:09.739
We happened to have a guy on who was

00:23:09.739 --> 00:23:13.069
talking about how he had an affair with
his wife.

00:23:13.069 --> 00:23:17.039
And he was crazy enough to come on, with
his wife, and his girlfriend.

00:23:17.039 --> 00:23:18.762
People ask me, why do people do that.

00:23:18.762 --> 00:23:21.869
It's because, nobody ever asked him so.

00:23:21.869 --> 00:23:24.828
[LAUGH] You say, would you come on with
your wife and girlfriend?

00:23:24.828 --> 00:23:29.472
He goes sure
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH] He was thinking.

00:23:29.472 --> 00:23:30.112
&gt;&gt; He was thinking.

00:23:30.112 --> 00:23:32.262
So, he comes on with the wife and the
girlfriend.

00:23:32.262 --> 00:23:34.219
This is the life-changing moment for me.

00:23:34.219 --> 00:23:36.084
The Klan, and this woman.

00:23:36.084 --> 00:23:37.424
The wife is there.

00:23:37.424 --> 00:23:39.486
He's in the center, and the girlfriend.

00:23:39.486 --> 00:23:41.652
And he tells his wife, he announces.

00:23:41.652 --> 00:23:43.613
We were live television at the time.

00:23:43.613 --> 00:23:47.508
And he announced that, to, to, to the
world

00:23:47.508 --> 00:23:52.031
and to his wife, that his girlfriend was
pregnant.

00:23:52.031 --> 00:23:53.401
And I did, you see her face?

00:23:53.401 --> 00:23:54.309
Your mouth's open, right there.

00:23:54.309 --> 00:23:57.644
[LAUGH] I did exactly that.

00:23:57.644 --> 00:23:58.877
I went, oh my God!

00:23:58.877 --> 00:24:00.597
And you could hear the gasp in the
audience.

00:24:00.597 --> 00:24:03.443
And, they're like, and, I literally
really, it

00:24:03.443 --> 00:24:06.210
still makes my eyes water to think about
it.

00:24:06.210 --> 00:24:10.300
I looked at her face, and I felt her
humiliation.

00:24:10.300 --> 00:24:15.500
I felt her shame, I felt it, and I, said
never again.

00:24:15.500 --> 00:24:19.540
[COUGH] I will get outta television, if I
have to do this.

00:24:19.540 --> 00:24:21.815
And I went and I had a meeting with the
producers, cuz

00:24:21.815 --> 00:24:24.373
I just had the Klan before, now I got the
adulteress here.

00:24:24.373 --> 00:24:28.307
[LAUGH] And [LAUGH] some uplifting show, I
must say.

00:24:28.307 --> 00:24:32.860
[LAUGH] And I said to the producers, we
are gonna change.

00:24:32.860 --> 00:24:34.940
We're gonna turn this around.

00:24:34.940 --> 00:24:38.130
And I am no longer gonna be used by
television.

00:24:38.130 --> 00:24:40.510
I am going to use television.

00:24:40.510 --> 00:24:41.960
What a concept!

00:24:41.960 --> 00:24:44.841
I am gonna use television, as a force for,
for,

00:24:44.841 --> 00:24:47.381
I didn't say at the time for good, I said.

00:24:47.381 --> 00:24:49.678
You know, let's think about what we wanna
say to the world.

00:24:49.678 --> 00:24:50.771
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:24:50.771 --> 00:24:55.076
&gt;&gt; And how we wanna use this as a
platform, to speak to the world.

00:24:55.076 --> 00:24:57.361
How do we want to see the world change?

00:24:57.361 --> 00:25:00.625
How do we wanna impact to the world, and
then let

00:25:00.625 --> 00:25:04.956
all of our shows really, be focused, and
seated around that.

00:25:04.956 --> 00:25:07.358
I then said to the producers exactly what
I said to you backstage.

00:25:07.358 --> 00:25:09.084
&gt;&gt; Mm-hm.

00:25:09.084 --> 00:25:12.362
&gt;&gt; Do not bring me a show, unless you have

00:25:12.362 --> 00:25:17.080
fully thought out what is your intention
for doing it.

00:25:17.080 --> 00:25:21.911
Because, if there is, if, if, if there is
a religion, or a mantra, or

00:25:21.911 --> 00:25:26.938
law that I live by, I live by the third
law of motion in physics.

00:25:26.938 --> 00:25:29.596
Which is Stanford.

00:25:29.596 --> 00:25:35.804
Which is [LAUGH] for every action, there's
an equal and opposite reaction.

00:25:35.804 --> 00:25:38.896
That is, that is, that is, that is my
religion.

00:25:38.896 --> 00:25:42.950
I know that what I'm thinking, and
therefore gonna act on, is going to

00:25:42.950 --> 00:25:47.230
come back to me, in this, in a, in a, in a
circular motion.

00:25:47.230 --> 00:25:48.090
Just like gravity.

00:25:48.090 --> 00:25:50.077
Like what goes up comes down.

00:25:50.077 --> 00:25:56.244
And so, what also propels the action, is
