00:55:46.970 --> 00:55:50.910
Selflessness with selfishness.

00:55:50.910 --> 00:55:53.985
Why are you asking me that question?

00:55:53.985 --> 00:55:58.177
[LAUGH] It's kind of the tension between
putting

00:55:58.177 --> 00:56:03.330
yourself first and also, taking care of
others.

00:56:03.330 --> 00:56:03.830
Okay.

00:56:05.300 --> 00:56:06.800
Well, I would say this.

00:56:06.800 --> 00:56:09.068
There is no, you have no, well,

00:56:09.068 --> 00:56:12.470
everybody's heard the whole oxygen mask
thing.

00:56:12.470 --> 00:56:19.990
The truth is, you don't have anything to
give that you don't have.

00:56:19.990 --> 00:56:24.400
So you have to keep your own self full.

00:56:24.400 --> 00:56:26.110
That's your job.

00:56:26.110 --> 00:56:27.947
You know, one of my daughters is

00:56:27.947 --> 00:56:30.950
here today from Oprah Winfrey Leadership
Academy.

00:56:30.950 --> 00:56:32.628
Stand up Shenay, so everybody can see you.

00:56:32.628 --> 00:56:41.118
[SOUND] You're going to end your first
year soon.

00:56:41.118 --> 00:56:43.170
Oh my god, it's your first year.

00:56:43.170 --> 00:56:48.478
I say to my girls all of the time, that
you're

00:56:48.478 --> 00:56:53.369
real work is to figure out where your
power

00:56:53.369 --> 00:56:58.259
base is and to work on the alignment of
your

00:56:58.259 --> 00:57:03.151
personality, your gifts that you have to

00:57:03.151 --> 00:57:08.360
give with the real reason why you're here.

00:57:08.360 --> 00:57:12.995
That's the number one thing you have to
do, is to work

00:57:12.995 --> 00:57:18.050
on yourself and to fill yourself up and
keep your cup full.

00:57:18.050 --> 00:57:18.650
Keep yourself full.

00:57:18.650 --> 00:57:21.890
I used to be afraid of that.

00:57:24.830 --> 00:57:26.706
I used to be afraid, particularly, from
people

00:57:26.706 --> 00:57:28.460
who'd say, oh, she's so full of herself.

00:57:28.460 --> 00:57:29.840
Mm, she's so full of herself and now, I
embrace it.

00:57:29.840 --> 00:57:37.680
I consider it a compliment that I am full
of myself because only when you're full.

00:57:37.680 --> 00:57:38.650
I'm full, I'm overflowing.

00:57:40.130 --> 00:57:42.830
My cup runneth over.

00:57:42.830 --> 00:57:44.040
I have so much.

00:57:44.040 --> 00:57:47.260
I have so much to offer and so much to

00:57:47.260 --> 00:57:52.450
give and I am not afraid of honoring
myself, you know.

00:57:52.450 --> 00:57:54.710
It's miraculous when you think about it.

00:57:54.710 --> 00:57:57.770
First of all, for me, my father and mother
never married.

00:57:57.770 --> 00:58:00.330
They had sex one time underneath an oak
tree

00:58:00.330 --> 00:58:03.715
because she was wearing a poodle skirt in
1953.

00:58:03.715 --> 00:58:04.320
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH].

00:58:04.320 --> 00:58:07.900
&gt;&gt; And my dad to this day says, I wanna
know what was under that skirt.

00:58:07.900 --> 00:58:08.675
That's what I wanna know.

00:58:08.675 --> 00:58:14.140
[LAUGH]

00:58:14.140 --> 00:58:16.250
He wanted to know what was under the
skirt.

00:58:16.250 --> 00:58:18.600
They didn't really have a relationship.

00:58:18.600 --> 00:58:22.299
She wanted one but you know, he went under
the skirt

00:58:22.299 --> 00:58:26.272
and that was it and one time, under the
oak tree, bam.

00:58:26.272 --> 00:58:27.539
Renaissance.

00:58:27.539 --> 00:58:29.847
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Woman is born.

00:58:29.847 --> 00:58:32.340
&gt;&gt; That's why I know my life is bigger
than that.

00:58:32.340 --> 00:58:40.300
My life has to be bigger, as your is,
bigger than a moment, than a poodle skirt.

00:58:42.880 --> 00:58:44.230
It's much bigger.

00:58:44.230 --> 00:58:46.154
The design, the reason why I'm here is
much bigger

00:58:46.154 --> 00:58:48.590
than oh, I think I wanna see what's under
there.

00:58:48.590 --> 00:58:54.470
So the ability to take care of that, to
honor that, to honor yourself and that

00:58:54.470 --> 00:59:01.525
which is greater than yourself, that which
was the reason for your being here.

00:59:01.525 --> 00:59:07.690
There's no selflessness in that.

00:59:09.300 --> 00:59:12.705
Only through that do you have the ability
to offer yourself, your whole

00:59:12.705 --> 00:59:16.510
self, your full expression of who you are,
to the rest of the world.

00:59:16.510 --> 00:59:21.210
So I remember the very first time I had a
life coach.They weren't called

00:59:21.210 --> 00:59:26.001
that at the time but an expert on who
shared with our audience, the women.

00:59:26.001 --> 00:59:28.304
She did a list and say where are you on
the list?

00:59:28.304 --> 00:59:29.996
And literally, in that audience, women
booed her,

00:59:29.996 --> 00:59:31.680
when she said put yourself top of the
list.

00:59:31.680 --> 00:59:34.960
This was in 1992.

00:59:34.960 --> 00:59:40.650
In 1992, the idea of being top of your own
list, was people like, how dare she?

00:59:40.650 --> 00:59:42.540
She doesn't have children.

00:59:42.540 --> 00:59:46.290
I said, she didn't say abandon your
children and go running in the streets.

00:59:46.290 --> 00:59:50.340
She just said, put yourself at the top of
the list.

00:59:50.340 --> 00:59:51.870
Nurture yourself.

00:59:51.870 --> 00:59:52.660
Honor yourself.

00:59:52.660 --> 00:59:56.539
Stop the crazy mind chatter in your head
that tells you all the time that

00:59:56.539 --> 00:59:58.974
you're not good enough because that's the

00:59:58.974 --> 01:00:02.700
number one, I've found too, issue with
everybody.

01:00:02.700 --> 01:00:11.461
The reason people say, you know, how is
that?

01:00:11.461 --> 01:00:13.850
How is that?

01:00:13.850 --> 01:00:16.040
&gt;&gt; It's cuz you wanna know how do you
measure up.

01:00:16.040 --> 01:00:18.713
Well, to know that your just being here,
your just being

01:00:18.713 --> 01:00:22.221
here, however that sperm, bam, hit that
egg, however that occurred for

01:00:22.221 --> 01:00:24.837
you, that your being here is such a
miraculous thing and

01:00:24.837 --> 01:00:27.360
that your real job is to honor that, is to
honor that.

01:00:28.810 --> 01:00:31.650
And the sooner you figure that out, oh
wow, wow, I'm one of the lucky ones.

01:00:32.760 --> 01:00:34.650
I got to be here.

01:00:34.650 --> 01:00:40.603
So how do you continue to prepare yourself
to live out the highest,

01:00:40.603 --> 01:00:45.937
fullest, truest expression of yourself as
a human being?

01:00:45.937 --> 01:00:49.314
I jst wanna end with this: there are no
mistakes.

01:00:49.314 --> 01:00:53.926
There really aren't any, cuz you have a
supreme destiny.

01:00:53.926 --> 01:00:55.451
When you're in your little mind, in

01:00:55.451 --> 01:00:57.764
your little personality mind or you're not
centered,

01:00:57.764 --> 01:01:01.175
you really don't know who you are but you
come from something greater and bigger.

01:01:01.175 --> 01:01:03.100
We really all are the same.

01:01:03.100 --> 01:01:06.278
You don't know that, you get all
flustered, you get

01:01:06.278 --> 01:01:10.099
stressed all the time, wanting something
to be what it isn't.

01:01:10.099 --> 01:01:13.630
There's a supreme moment of destiny
calling on your life.

01:01:13.630 --> 01:01:16.796
Your job is to feel that, to hear that, to
know

01:01:16.796 --> 01:01:22.800
that and sometimes, when you're not
listening, you get taken off track.

01:01:22.800 --> 01:01:28.700
You get in the wrong marriage, the wrong
relationship, you take the wrong job.

01:01:28.700 --> 01:01:33.240
Yeah, but it's all leading to the same
path.

01:01:33.240 --> 01:01:34.350
There are no wrong paths.

01:01:34.350 --> 01:01:34.710
There are none.

01:01:34.710 --> 01:01:37.130
There's no such thing as failure really,
because failure is

01:01:37.130 --> 01:01:43.530
just that thing, trying to move you in
another direction.

01:01:43.530 --> 01:01:49.558
So you get as much from your losses, as
you do from

01:01:49.558 --> 01:01:56.100
your victory cuz the losses are there to
wake you up.

01:01:56.100 --> 01:01:58.752
The losses are to say, fool, that is why

01:01:58.752 --> 01:02:02.170
you go to school, so that CBS can call
you.

01:02:02.170 --> 01:02:07.648
So when you understand that you don't
allow yourself to be completely thrown

01:02:07.648 --> 01:02:12.028
by a grade or by a circumstance because
your life is bigger than

01:02:12.028 --> 01:02:16.241
any one experience and if I had, I always
ask people on Super

01:02:16.241 --> 01:02:21.570
Soul Sunday to tell me, what would you say
to your younger self?

01:02:21.570 --> 01:02:30.315
Every person says in one form or another,
I would have said, relax.

01:02:30.315 --> 01:02:31.530
&gt;&gt; [COUGH]
&gt;&gt; Relax.

01:02:31.530 --> 01:02:31.960
It's gonna be okay.

01:02:31.960 --> 01:02:35.017
It really is gonna be okay because even if
you're on

01:02:35.017 --> 01:02:38.429
a detour right now and that's how you
know, when you're

01:02:38.429 --> 01:02:42.409
not at ease with yourself, when you're
feeling like [SOUND], that

01:02:42.409 --> 01:02:45.919
is the cue that you need to be moving in
another direction.

01:02:45.919 --> 01:02:50.970
Don't let yourself get all thrown off,
continue to be thrown off course.

01:02:50.970 --> 01:02:53.610
When you're feeling off course, that's the
key.

01:02:53.610 --> 01:02:55.070
How do I turn around?

01:02:55.070 --> 01:03:00.743
So when everybody was talking about, when
I started this network,

01:03:00.743 --> 01:03:05.731
if I had only known, good lord, how
difficult it would be.

01:03:05.731 --> 01:03:08.781
The way through the challenge is to get
still

01:03:08.781 --> 01:03:11.923
and ask yourself what is the next right
move?

01:03:11.923 --> 01:03:15.843
Not think about oh, I got all of this to,
what is

01:03:15.843 --> 01:03:20.449
the next right move and then from that
space make the next

01:03:20.449 --> 01:03:25.448
right move and the next right move and not
to be overwhelmed by

01:03:25.448 --> 01:03:30.472
it because you know your life is bigger
than that one moment.

01:03:30.472 --> 01:03:33.529
You know you're not defined by what
somebody

01:03:33.529 --> 01:03:36.424
says is a failure for you because failure
is

01:03:36.424 --> 01:03:39.641
just there to point you in a different
direction

01:03:39.641 --> 01:03:42.390
and that's all the time I got right now.

01:03:42.390 --> 01:03:42.630
&gt;&gt; Thank you.

01:03:42.630 --> 01:03:42.760
Yeah.

01:03:42.760 --> 01:03:42.865
&gt;&gt; Thank you.

